l binning has been around  for a very long time but what makes it  special is the innovative technologies  inside the a16 bionic chip the a16  bionic now has an intelligent processor  specifically designed to bin these  pixels that means as more photos are  taken throughout the iphone network the  smarter this system is going to get the  better the ai is going to get and the  better your photos are progressively  going to get over time now nobody can  guarantee that the photo taken today  will be better than the photo taken  tomorrow but in layman's terms that is  the overall intention behind pixel  binning through an ai system in the a16  bionic chip you might be thinking as  well great we have three cameras on the  back like we always have what's the  difference well the 48 megapixel main  sensor is now a 24 millimeter focal  length with a 48 millimeter focal length  when you go to 2x zoom again david stop  using all these big terms and start  explaining it in layman's terms  basically the 24 millimeter and the 48  millimeter lenses are critical in  photography most photographers will use  anything from a 16 mil to a 24  millimeter to capture the perfect  landscape shot whilst they'll go all the  way up to a 50 millimeter to capture the  perfect portrait so in your back pocket  now you have a 24 millimeter and a 48  millimeter both in that  megapixel camera system with the larger  sensor that can take amazing photos for  either landscape or portrait not to  mention the ultra wide camera is also a  macro camera that means you're allowed  to come as close as you want to be able  to define those subjects and define  those details as we all know architects  love to get up close and personal with  their details and we truly love to  capture the finest details we possibly  can now here's where it gets interesting  imagine you're out on site somewhere in  the middle of nowhere typical remote  australia you're walking through the  long grass and a nostalgic sound place  a